/T (2. Correlation Heatmap Question: Which variables are connected with book popularity? The correlation heatmap helps us understand the relationship between numerical variables: downloads, days online, and title length. This graph is useful because it quickly shows whether one variable increases or decreases together with another variable. For example, if downloads and days online have a positive correlation, it means that books that have been available longer may have more downloads. At the same time, the heatmap helps us check whether title length has any noticeable connection with downloads. If the correlation is weak, it means that the number of words in a title does not strongly affect popularity. Overall, this graph gives a quick overview of which factors may be important and which ones are less influential.)
